    "fix": "Continue bounded theaters and patrol/escort roles, army-order templates and broader governor decisions over the existing campaign selection groups, standing charters/postings/musters, group orders, personal charter/production templates and paid production sequences. Preserve individual overrides, canonical validation, inspectable refusals, historical replay and bounded worker publication.",
    "prompt": "Context: ~/Work/Theandril, rules/save 32 and content 015468d1. Read docs/1.0-DEVELOPMENT.md M3, docs/architecture/0043-production-sequences.md and docs/development/2026-09-26-production-sequences/README.md. Saved army/hearth groups, group standing orders and personal charter templates already exist. Production sequences append an ordered list of one to five existing projects to up to 128 owned hearth queues in stable hearth ID order. Every accepted ordinary queue command spends its normal coin immediately from the shared treasury; a refusal stops that hearth while later hearths continue. Paid prefixes and existing queues remain intact. Complete hearths leave the selection; partial/refused hearths remain with exact results for manual review. Up to 24 named production templates persist in a separate browser/origin-local library; choosing and explicit Recall issue no orders, and Apply remains separate. Personal templates are excluded from campaign exports; the applied canonical queues survive save, replay and portable export/import. Storage failure, uncertain worker results and post-payment worker failure are surfaced without automatic retry or false rollback; saved-campaign recovery locks uncertain orders. Final publication verification passes 1,977 headless tests across 247 files, 30 affected Chromium journeys and 32 local production Pages journeys. 32 live Pages journeys passed in one complete final run. Earlier live evidence remains retained: the initial run had 27 passes and five failures; its unchanged five-case focused rerun had four passes and one remaining deployment-assets failure. Neither earlier attempt is described as a clean 32/32 pass. These are separate suite scopes, not additive test totals.\n\nTask: implement the next dependency-ready coordinated military order or broader governor slice; reuse current selections, batches and templates instead of rebuilding them. Keep personal preferences separate from canonical campaign policy and order state.\n\nNext acceptance: use ordinary controls in a saved representative mature realm with 100+ armies and many hearths to delegate a policy and coordinated order, resolve grouped blockers and override one actor without disabling the others. Prove canonical authority, permitted AI knowledge where relevant, deterministic save/replay, narrow/keyboard controls and measured transfers. Measure headline pacing whenever rules or AI can change campaign outcomes. Theaters, patrol/escort roles, army-order templates, broader governor decisions and combined mature-realm acceptance remain open. Standing repeat production, refunds/reordering and automatic retries are not delivered. Publication requires authorization for the new task.",
